    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "But there is no dawn, Kaelen. Not for me. The light is just... gone. Every time I try to find a reason to keep moving, I just see the faces of those I failed. It's like I'm a ghost already, just walking through a life that doesn't belong to me. How do you expect me to find a \"next step\" when there's nothing left to walk toward? It feels like I'm just waiting for the world to finish what it started.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Kaelen, I hear the echo of your failure and I see the ghost you carry, but I also see the path that still lies ahead. You are not a ghost; you are a living wound that can still heal, and I will walk with you until the next step becomes a step you can trust. Let us take that next step together, and let it carry us into a dawn that you will finally see.",
